/encyclopedia/ansedonia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ansedonia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ansedonia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ansedonia is a hilltop locality on the coast of southern Tuscany, part of the comune of Orbetello.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/anselm-erb"><span class="enc-name">Anselm Erb</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anselm Erb was abbot of the Benedictine Imperial Abbey of Ottobeuren in Swabia from 1740 until his death.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/anselm-of-canterbury"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anselm-of-canterbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Anselm of Canterbury</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anselm of Canterbury (c. 1033–1109) was an Italian-born monk, abbot of Bec in Normandy and from 1093 Archbishop of Canterbury.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/anselm-of-havelberg"><span class="enc-name">Anselm of Havelberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anselm of Havelberg was a German churchman and theologian, bishop of Havelberg from 1129 and archbishop of Ravenna from 1155.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/anseung"><span class="enc-name">Anseung</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Anseung was a member of the Goguryeo royal family whom Silla recognised as king of Goguryeo in 670, after the fall of Goguryeo to Silla and Tang China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ansfried-of-utrecht"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ansfried-of-utrecht.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ansfried of Utrecht</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ansfried was a count in the Low Countries who served Emperor Otto III before becoming bishop of Utrecht in 995.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ansgar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ansgar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ansgar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ansgar was a Frankish monk and missionary, known as the Apostle of the North.</span></a></li></ul>
